<title>GERMANY: REUTERS' 1ST EX-FRANKFURT ASIA/MIDEAST REPORT.</title>
<headline>REUTERS' 1ST EX-FRANKFURT ASIA/MIDEAST REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-Frankfurt (FRA) German mark air cargo rates per kg for a 100kg shipment, with a volume to weight ratio of six-to-one. These rates are exclusive of the cargo fuel surcharges being applied by airlines.</p>
<p>			 Mar 5     Dec 24</p>
<p>			  ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p>    FRA-BKK	  2.80	2.70</p>
<p>    FRA-KUL	  2.85	2.75</p>
<p>    FRA-HKG	  2.95	2.85</p>
<p>    FRA-NRT	  4.60	4.35</p>
<p>    FRA-SEL	  3.90	3.80</p>
<p>    FRA-SHA	  3.30	3.20</p>
<p>    FRA-SIN	  2.85	2.75</p>
<p>    FRA-TPE	  2.60	n/a</p>
<p>			   MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p>    FRA-DXB	  1.55	1.45</p>
<p>		     INDIAN SUB-CONTINENT</p>
<p>    FRA-BOM	  1.85	n/a</p>
<p>* The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuter journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at or near Frankfurt Airport.</p>
<p>* All prices are quoted in German marks.</p>
<p>* The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices, including standard, discount and spot rates, and are indicative of current market activity.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
